        "original_id": "72d7390f-827f-5f43-922e-253aae88529b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: The Strongest Man in the World, Candleshoe, Now You See Him, Now You Don't, The Computer Wore Tennis Shoes\n- People: Kurt Russell, Jodie Foster, David Niven, Helen Hayes, Leo McKern, Michael Innes\n- Organizations: Disney, Walt Disney Productions\n- Places: Medfield College\n- Concepts: sequels, adaptations\n\nFacts:\n- \"The Computer Wore Tennis Shoes\" is a 1969 film that was followed by the sequel \"Now You See Him, Now You Don't.\"\n- \"The Strongest Man in the World\" followed \"Now You See Him, Now You Don't\" in 1975.\n- \"The Strongest Man in the World\" is a 1975 Disney film starring Kurt Russell as a student at the fictional Medfield College.\n- \"Candleshoe\" is a 1977 American family adventure film produced by Walt Disney Productions.\n- \"Candleshoe\" is based on Michael Innes's novel \"Christmas at Candleshoe.\"\n- \"Candleshoe\" stars Jodie Foster, David Niven, Helen Hayes, and Leo McKern.\n- \"Candleshoe\" was Helen Hayes's last big-screen appearance.",
